Z||000000||BENGAL4||12-01-1999||11:26 AM||||I have found a 1974 350V8 with a Gary Zumalt kit, 4 speed on a Fiero cradle all ready to be installed. The engine has a new cam & head work, headers etc. The guy was going to build a kit car but lost interest. <P>My problem is that in order to do this legally, the car will have to pass 1986 emission standards. My question is has anybody on the Forum heard of putting emission equipment on pre 1975 engines.<P>If this was going into a kit car, the state would grant a permanent exemption. But since this is an 86GT, they will not.<P>Any input would be appreciated. And I will only do this swap legally.<P><BR>||||reg||5
