Z||000007||ChadMan||12-02-1999||10:13 AM||||E-checks are not statewide in Ohio, but the lefties keep trying and trying to make it so.  <P>With new-car emissions getting cleaner and cleaner, I simply don't think it's worth the enviro benefit to force owners of older cars to shell out for expensive repairs in order to meet e-check standards.  This hits the working poor right in the pocketbook.  Most of us drive old Pontiacs because we want to, but I'd guess most people driving 80's-vintage cars do it because they have to.<P>Vote ChadMan in '00!||||reg||1
